## v0.3 Week 19 Thu — Architect agent.
##
## Reads a natural-language feature spec + emits a structured
## aiSlang resource-block design (5-section markdown — see
## prompts/architect.md for the contract).  Downstream agents
## (Coder, Reviewer — Fri) consume the markdown directly.
##
## ## Direct chat (iterate on the design)
##
## ```
## aislang chat architect examples/agents/architect/architect.ais
## > Design a `dataset` block for declaring training data
##   (path + format fields, fits the existing v0.3 grammar).
## ```
##
## Refine through dialogue; once happy, copy the design out for
## downstream use.  Week 19 Fri ships standalone Coder + Reviewer
## agents (`examples/agents/coder/` + `code_reviewer/`); Week 20
## Mon's orchestrator agent chains them via cross-module
## pipeline.steps (Architect → Coder → Code-reviewer); Tue extends
## the chain to add the Tester leg.
##
## ## End-to-end pipeline (one-shot)
##
## Week 19 Thu/Fri ship each agent standalone — the `full_design`
## pipeline below remains a single-step placeholder.  Week 20 Mon's
## `examples/agents/orchestrator.ais` multi-module project wires
## the full chain end-to-end.
##
## ## RAG context
##
## The agent declares `knowledge = [vector_store.architect_kb]`.
## `aislang apply` builds the index from `./knowledge/` (LANGUAGE-
## SPEC excerpts + Decisions 44.x + AST shapes + exemplar .ais);
## chat-time each user message embeds via bge-m3 + top-4 chunks
## prepend to the system prompt.  Verifiable in Jaeger: the
## `aislang.system_prompt` span attribute shows the retrieved
## context inline.
##
## ## Model choice (deviates from Decision 44.8)
##
## PLAN row 19-Thu locked Qwen2.5-Coder.  Amended at Thu planning
## review: Architect designs (not code-generates), so reasoning-
## capable Qwen3 8B is better suited.  Qwen2.5-Coder reserved for
## Fri's Coder agent which actually emits Rust.  anthropic.haiku
## fallback when Ollama is unavailable.

project "architect-agent" {
  budget {
    hard_cap_per_day = $1
    hard_cap_per_run = $0.50
  }

  ## Cloud-tier reasoning model for design work.  Haiku is the
  ## primary because CPU-bound qwen3:8b inference comfortably
  ## exceeds the LiteLLM client's 5-minute ceiling on commodity
  ## hardware; Ollama qwen3:8b stays declared as a local fallback
  ## for the GPU case (when AISLANG_LITELLM_TIMEOUT_SECS isn't
  ## needed) — the same reasoning-tier model, just slower without
  ## hardware acceleration.  Original "qwen3 primary" pre-dated
  ## the user's CPU-inference reality check (Week 20 Mon follow-up).
  model "architect_brain" {
    requires    = [chat]
    context_min = 32k
    prefer      = [anthropic.claude_haiku_4_5]
    fallback    = [ollama.qwen3_8b]
  }

  embedding "local_bge" {
    provider = ollama
    model    = "bge-m3:latest"
  }

  vector_store "architect_kb" {
    embedding     = embedding.local_bge
    source        = "./knowledge/"
    chunk_size    = 768
    chunk_overlap = 96
  }

  prompt "architect_sys" {
    file    = "./prompts/architect.md"
    version = "1.0.1"
  }

  agent "architect" {
    model         = model.architect_brain
    system_prompt = prompt.architect_sys
    tools         = []
    knowledge     = [vector_store.architect_kb]
  }

  ## Single-step pipeline removed in W20 Mon follow-up: the real
  ## 3-agent chain lives in `examples/agents/orchestrator/` (use
  ## `aislang chat full_design examples/agents/orchestrator/`).
  ## Keeping a same-named placeholder here caused an ambiguous
  ## suffix-match with the orchestrator's real pipeline when the
  ## user typed unqualified `full_design` against the orchestrator
  ## dir.  For the standalone "iterate on a design" workflow,
  ## chat against `agent.architect` directly — no pipeline
  ## wrapper needed.

  ## Heuristic eval — 3 synthetic specs check that the Architect
  ## emits the 5-section structure + a fenced grammar block.
  ## SonarQube-driven quality-of-implementation eval deferred to
  ## v0.5+ — see PLAN-v0_3.md "Out of scope" §
  ## ("External quality-gate tools consulted by Reviewer / Tester
  ## via MCP") for the full deferral rationale.
  eval "structured_output" {
    dataset   = "./evals/architect_specs.jsonl"
    metric    = f1
    threshold = 80%
    agent     = agent.architect
  }

  deploy "local" {
    target = compose
  }
}
